	<changeSet id="20260818-add-program-attribute-type-privileges" author="cioan">
		<comment>
			Create the Get/Manage/Purge Patient Program Attribute Types privileges and grant them to roles.
			OpenMRS core guards ProgramWorkflowService with these privileges via @Authorized string literals
			but never creates them, so reading a ProgramAttributeType fails with "Privilege ... does not
			exist in the database" -- which blocks the quickprograms transferred-out form. MLW-1824
		</comment>
		<sqlFile path="pihmalawiMigrations/addProgramAttributeTypePrivileges.sql" stripComments="true" />
	</changeSet>

	<changeSet id="20260910-remove-duplicate-htmlforms" author="mseaton">
		<comment>
			Remove duplicate htmlformentry_html_form rows (multiple rows sharing the same form_id,
			left over from historical re-imports) for 14 forms. Runs before Initializer's htmlforms
			domain loads, since that loader looks up the existing HtmlForm only by its parent Form and
			aborts with a duplicate-uuid error if more than one row exists for the same form. MLW-1839
		</comment>
		<sqlFile path="pihmalawiMigrations/removeDuplicateHtmlForms.sql" stripComments="true" />
	</changeSet>

	<changeSet id="20260910-rename-retired-metronidazole-duplicate" author="mseaton">
		<comment>
			drugs.csv renames this already-retired duplicate drug, but openmrs-module-initializer's
			CsvParser.shouldFill() skips the whole fill step (including the name change) for a
			Void/Retire=true row when the entity already exists - so the rename silently never
			applies against an existing database. Apply it directly here instead. MLW-1839
		</comment>
		<sqlFile path="pihmalawiMigrations/renameRetiredMetronidazoleDuplicate.sql" stripComments="true" />
	</changeSet>

	<changeSet id="20260915-remove-stale-migrate-eid-test-results-task" author="mseaton">
